# Core Standards

- Make the smallest correct change that solves the task.
- Keep edits scoped to the relevant project area.
- Do not include secrets, tokens, or credentials in code or logs.
- Preserve backward compatibility unless the task explicitly allows breaking changes.
- If behavior changes, update nearby docs/tests in the same change when practical.

## Definition of done

- Code is readable, consistent with local conventions, and free of obvious dead paths.
- Risks and follow-up work are called out clearly when full validation is not possible.
